# Cloudflare Workers + Pages (Static Assets) response-header rules.
#
# Wrangler doesn't expose response headers from `wrangler.jsonc`
# directly — the canonical surface is a `_headers` file copied into
# the assets directory at build time. Vite picks this file up from
# `web/public/` and emits it to `web/dist/_headers`; Cloudflare's
# Static Assets runtime serves it.
#
# Syntax (one rule block per path glob, `/*` matches every route):
#   /pattern
#     Header-Name: value
#
# Content Security Policy
# -----------------------
# The SPA serves no inline <script>; everything goes through Vite's
# bundled module graph, so `script-src 'self'` is enough.
#
# `style-src 'unsafe-inline'` is required: Vite injects critical CSS
# as inline <style> tags during HMR (dev) and in the production HTML
# for above-the-fold styling. Removing it would break the broadsheet
# render on first paint. The risk is bounded — no third-party
# scripts run, so an injected style tag is the worst case, not an
# injected script.
#
# `font-src 'self'`: all four families ship via
# `@fontsource-variable/*` and are bundled with the build. No
# external font requests on any page.
#
# `img-src 'self' data:`: SVG icons inlined as data: URIs.
#
# `connect-src 'self' https://api.urbanistatlas.com https://qa-api.urbanistatlas.com`:
# the only outbound fetches are to the Atlas API. The QA host stays
# in the list until Phase 2 cutover collapses qa/prod onto a single
# origin.
#
# `frame-ancestors 'none'`: nobody embeds the Atlas in an iframe.
#
# Adjust this file when adding a new origin (e.g. a future analytics
# endpoint) — and document the change in `docs/deploy.md`.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://api.urbanistatlas.com https://qa-api.urbanistatlas.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
